            "quote": "Our hypothesis is that inhibition of this mechanism, which is not widespread in most tissues and at the same time is common to several steps of cancer-induced osteolysis (i.e., homing, growth, and survival of metastatic cells, osteoclast bone resorption, and angiogenesis), should represent a suitable target to block the development of bone spreading of metastatic tumors. We extend this hypothesis to downstream signalling molecules activated by ligation of the alphaVbeta3 integrin, some of which (i.e., Src, PYK2, and Shc) could have similar specific roles in tumor cells, activated endothelium and osteoclasts, but not in other cell types.",
